## Root cause

The pool size was edited in a shared configuration file and deployed to every pod at once. Twenty connections could not serve peak Billing API traffic, so request threads blocked waiting for a free connection until they hit their timeout. Nothing in the review or deploy path flagged that the new value was an order of magnitude below the previous one.

! The config linter did not validate pool size bounds, so the out-of-range value passed every check.

## Action items

